From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyroshine Vendor Maintenance <vendor@pyroshine.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:12:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Allow compute-only contexts on a selected device without
 Vulkan Video encode

Encode support now requires the VK_KHR_video_queue and
VK_KHR_video_encode_queue extensions in addition to a VIDEO_ENCODE queue
family: ANV on Xe2 and newer reports such a queue family with
ANV_DEBUG=video-encode but exposes no encode extensions, and device creation
failed. Each unsupported codec records the first missing requirement
(encode_unsupported_reason). allow_without_encode() accepts the selected
device without encode, creating compute/transfer queues only, so callers
can still convert and import external memory on it. The video queue
extension is enabled only with an encode queue.
---
